<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kampen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kampen is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> province of Overijssel, near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ijssel">IJssel</a>. In the 14th and 15th centuries it was one of the wealthiest towns of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, a Hanseatic port trading with the Baltic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. The silting of the river brought decline from the 16th century, which has preserved much of its medieval town centre, gates and riverside front.</p></div>
